      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Step 5: Handling the \"Divide By 0\" Exception"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "By now, you already know that dividing by 0 causes an exception in C++. So, we will be handling this exception in this section."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In the formula for complex division, the denominator is given by the sum of the squares of the real and imaginary parts of the divisor."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Deriving the formula for complex division",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In the image above, the divisor is c + di. So, the denominator in the formula is given by c ^ 2 + d ^ 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Thus, the denominator becomes 0 when both c and d are 0 i.e. when both the real and imag attributes of the complex2 object are 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, let's see how we can handle such an exception:"
    },
    {
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "items": [
        "First, we'll use the try...catch block inside the overloaded / operator.",
        "Since there's already a denominator variable that calculates the sum of the required squares, we'll simply throw an exception when denominator == 0.",
        "In the catch block, we'll print an error message and exit the program."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "Complex operator / (Complex arg) {\n        \n    Complex complex_division;\n\n\n    try {\n\n\n        double denominator = pow(arg.real, 2) + pow(arg.imag, 2);\n        \n\n        // throw an exception if denominator is 0    \n        if (denominator == 0)\n            throw 0;\n\n\n        // use complex division formula\n        complex_division.real = ((this->real * arg.real) + (this->imag * arg.imag)) / denominator;\n        complex_division.imag = ((this->imag * arg.real) - (this->real * arg.imag)) / denominator;\n    }\n\n\n    catch (int num) {\n\n        // print the error message and exit the program\n        cout << \"Error! Cannot divide by \" << num << endl;\n        exit(0);\n    }\n\n       \n    return complex_division;\n}"
    },
    {
